
<section class="rounded-[26px] border border-red-200 bg-red-50/60 p-6 sm:p-8"
         role="alert"
         aria-labelledby="graph-error-title">

  <div class="flex items-start gap-4">
    <div class="flex h-12 w-12 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-2xl border border-red-200 bg-white text-xl">⚠️</div>

    <div class="min-w-0 flex-1">
      <p class="text-[10px] font-black uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-red-700">Request failure</p>
      <h2 id="graph-error-title" class="mt-1 text-lg font-black text-red-950">The graph could not be loaded</h2>

      <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-red-800">
        The server could not complete the graph-loading workflow. The fallback display is not proof that the database contains no data.
      </p>

      <div class="mt-4 rounded-xl border border-red-200 bg-white/80 p-4">
        <p class="text-xs font-black text-red-900">Administrator checklist</p>
        <ul class="mt-2 list-disc space-y-1 pl-5 text-xs leading-6 text-red-800">
          <li>Inspect Rails logs for the original exception.</li>
          <li>Identify which graph, metrics, diagnostics, or candidate service failed.</li>
          <li>Verify the expected hash and array structures.</li>
          <li>Check browser developer tools for JavaScript errors.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <button type="button"
              class="mt-5 rounded-xl bg-red-800 px-4 py-3 text-sm font-bold text-white hover:bg-red-900"
              data-action="click->relationship-graph#reload">
        Try again
      </button>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>